          ],
          "level": 1,
          "content": "ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.376,
            0.279,
            0.396
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "5.1 Introduction"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.407,
            0.898,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": "**You must have observed that in nature, many things follow a certain pattern, such as the petals of a sunflower, the holes of a honeycomb, the grains on a maize cob, the spirals on a pineapple and on a pine cone, etc.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.47,
            0.899,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": "**We now look for some patterns which occur in our day-to-day life. Some such examples are :**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.514,
            0.595,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": "**(i) Reena applied for a job and got selected. She has been offered a job with a starting monthly salary of** \\` **8000, with an annual increment of** \\` **500 in her salary. Her salary (in** \\`**) for the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, . . . years will be, respectively** 8000, 8500, 9000,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.642,
            0.593,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": "**(ii) The lengths of the rungs of a ladder decrease uniformly by 2 cm from bottom to top (see Fig. 5.1). The bottom rung is 45 cm in length. The lengths (in cm) of the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, . . ., 8th rung from the bottom to the top are, respectively**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.673,
            0.517,
            0.833,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.715,
                0.747,
                0.798,
                0.767
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.1"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.763,
            0.509,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "**45, 43, 41, 39, 37, 35, 33, 31**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.796,
            0.899,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": "**(iii) In a savings scheme, the amount becomes** $\\frac { 5 } { 4 }$ **times of itself after every 3 years. The maturity amount (in** \\`**) of an investment of** \\` **8000 after 3, 6, 9 and 12 years will be, respectively :**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.238,
            0.877,
            0.58,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": "**10000, 12500, 15625, 19531.25**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
